\title{A Vec can be read with a fallback in one call}
\taxon{Change}
\date{2026-11-17}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{stdlib}
\tag{unreleased}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{pr}{1088}
\import{base-macros}

\p{\code{\verb~|Vec::get_or(index, otherwise)~} is new on the copy-on-write \code{\verb~|Vec~}: the element at \code{\verb~|index~}, or \code{\verb~|otherwise~} past the end. It is one call into the runtime and builds no option, where \code{\verb~|get(index).unwrap_or(otherwise)~} is two calls, an allocation and a release, about a hundred instructions for a scalar. \code{\verb~|get~} is unchanged. The steps that build a regex automaton read their vectors with it. See [the session](ses-A1OD).}

\p{In review as \pr{1088}.}
